hexagon: the host matcher gives the conv chunk the snapshot slots of a batch

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus the patches before this one in patches/series.

Needs patches/hexagon-spec/0001 before it, which makes the conv chunk kernel write K slots.
Without that kernel the fused op writes one window into every slot and the conv state of a
rollback is wrong.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h   the refusal of a batch with several snapshot slots

The problem

patches/hexagon-spec/0001 makes gdn-conv-ops.c write K slots of the conv cache on a batch, and
its kernel context takes n_slots and slot_stride. Nothing reaches that code, because the host
matcher refuses the chain first:

    if (cpys.size() > 1 && n_tokens > 1) {
        return "more than one CPY of the CONCAT on a batch (rollback snapshots)";
    }

The refusal comes from patches/hexagon-fusion/0007, where the batch kernel wrote one slot. Thus
GDN_CONV_CHUNK is never emitted while the context keeps rollback slots, and the conv work of
patches/hexagon-kernels is dead on that path.

The change

The refusal goes. Nothing else in the matcher needs a change:

  - The loop that follows already checks the window of each slot at any token count. It takes
    the column max(0, n_tokens - g) for slot g, which is the column that build_conv_state writes
    (s_idx = max(0, n_seq_tokens - s_slot)), and it checks that the slots are evenly strided.
  - Every CPY is already a member of the chain, thus ggml_hexagon_gdn_chain_is_private and
    ggml_hexagon_gdn_chain_span_is_clean already cover them.
  - ggml_hexagon_match_gdn_fusions already builds the span tensor whenever n_slots is more than
    one, with n_slots rows and the slot stride, and it does not look at the token count.

The comment above the loop carried the old reason. It now states that the batch takes the same
path and that the kernel reads the slot count and the slot stride from the span.

What still refuses

A batch with one slot is unchanged. A chain whose slots are not evenly strided, or whose windows
are not the expected columns, still refuses, and the unfused nodes run.

With patches/hexagon-spec/0003 a prompt ubatch writes one slot, thus this patch is not what gives
the prefill its speed. It gives the conv chunk to a multi-token ubatch that keeps its slots,
which is the verify step of speculative decoding.

State of the verification

The Android build of the pinned container compiles the change. The device has not run it. The
device check is a prefill with speculation on and GGML_HEXAGON_VERBOSE set: the line
"fused GDN_CONV_CHUNK" must appear for each linear layer, and the answer must not move.
